@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-apply-patches-to-an-isolated-json-clone
+type: decision-log
+title: "Apply patches to an isolated JSON clone"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 operations are sequential and may alter nested arrays and objects. The public API promises
+not to mutate its input and must throw if an operation fails.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate that the document and patch values are JSON values, deep-clone the document before applying
+operations, and mutate only that private working copy. Object comparisons for `test` use structural
+JSON equality, including object members independent of insertion order.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Successful calls return an independent JSON value. A failed operation throws without changing the
+caller-owned input; no rollback machinery is needed because the partial state is private.
